{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1777551894,"nonce":"K6W8uZbZMVTscvFD/sGKeYG4Jfg=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABA5j7kc62u4-f"},"target":"f40e09ab0eaa46b6bfc7da6815a0ef8eb9cb808e1bf5f96f7ef6833a983db2d7","message":"## Summary\n\n`bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml` configures `mru_transform` to use\n`mavros/global_position/global` as its position source (the FCU EKF3-fused\noutput), but the corresponding `logger` block does not record that topic.\nToday's in-water deployment (#104) bag therefore captured the FCU's raw\n`global_position/raw/fix` and `raw/gps_vel` but **not** the actual position\nstream the platform's nav stack is fusing.\n\nThe same gap applies to the rest of the EKF3-fused mavros family —\n`local_position/*` and `altitude` — none of which are being recorded.\nCross-checking SBG against \"the FCU's nav output\" therefore had to fall\nback to `/bizzy/odom` (downstream of `mru_transform`) instead of the\nactual EKF3 streams, which loses signal about anything `mru_transform`\nitself transforms.\n\n## Evidence\n\n`bizzyboat.yaml`:\n\n- Lines 24–25 (default `mru_transform` config) and 42–43 (override) set\n  `position: \"mavros/global_position/global\"`.\n- Lines 141 / 208 declare `mavros_position_ekf: {source: mavros/global_position/global}`\n  as a named candidate source.\n- Logger topics list (lines 215–267) currently includes\n  `/bizzy/mavros/global_position/raw/fix` and `raw/gps_vel`, but **not**\n  `/bizzy/mavros/global_position/global`, nor any `/bizzy/mavros/local_position/*`,\n  nor `/bizzy/mavros/altitude`.\n- udp_bridge config in the same file already pulls\n  `mavros/local_position/velocity_body` (line 207), confirming the\n  `local_position` plugin is loaded and publishing.\n\nConfirmed missing in `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/2026-04-29T21-43-29+00-00`\n(`ros2 bag info` topic list does not contain any of the above).\n\nThis is BizzyBoat-specific. `izzyboat_project11/config/izzyboat.yaml` still\nuses `mavros/global_position/raw/fix` as the mru_transform position source\n(line 20), so its recorder list is consistent with what's actually fused.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd to the BizzyBoat logger topics list, near the other `mavros/*` entries:\n\n- `/bizzy/mavros/global_position/global` — EKF3-fused global position\n  (the actual `mru_transform` source)\n- `/bizzy/mavros/local_position/pose` — EKF3-fused local pose\n- `/bizzy/mavros/local_position/velocity_local` — EKF3-fused velocity (NED)\n- `/bizzy/mavros/local_position/velocity_body` — EKF3-fused velocity (FRD/body);\n  already used by udp_bridge so the plugin is up\n- `/bizzy/mavros/altitude` — fused altitude (only if the `altitude`\n  plugin is loaded by current bizzyboat plugin set; verify before adding,\n  or accept that an unloaded topic just records nothing)\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- All five topics present in the next BizzyBoat bag's `ros2 bag info`\n  output (or, for `altitude`, a note that the plugin isn't loaded so\n  nothing was published).\n- `mru_transform` continues to fuse `global_position/global` as before\n  (no behavior change — this is a recording-only fix).\n- Next deployment's SBG-vs-FCU cross-check can compare against the\n  actual EKF3 streams instead of `/bizzy/odom`.\n\n## References\n\n- Discovered while cross-checking SBG vs mavros EKF on the 2026-04-29 bag —\n  see `docs/logs/2026/2026-04-29_dev_logs.md` (timeline entry\n  2026-04-30T00:06-04:00).\n- Related: #104 (deployment), #110 (URDF SBG modelling),\n  #111 (lever-arm/base_link contract). #110/#111/#112 form the\n  \"both nav systems report at base_link\" group on the roadmap.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1777523626,"nonce":"DtW4t6wac5VZoV+XVN+v8BYdmGI=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABA5j7kc8AAAAF0znSMA"},"added":["bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":4,"timestamp":1777592124,"nonce":"14AIsiT